CPopulationManager keeps its parsed waves in the private m_waveVector and exposes
only GetTotalWaveCount() and GetCurrentWave(), because the game itself never needs
any other wave. CWave::GetNextWave() is declared in tf_populators.h but the Source
SDK 2013 release ships no definition for it, so walking the list that way does not
link.

GetWave() is an additive const-style read accessor over the existing vector. It
changes no behaviour and is used only by shim/entsapi.cpp to report every parsed
wave to the host.

diff --git a/src/game/server/tf/player_vs_environment/tf_population_manager.h b/src/game/server/tf/player_vs_environment/tf_population_manager.h
--- a/src/game/server/tf/player_vs_environment/tf_population_manager.h
+++ b/src/game/server/tf/player_vs_environment/tf_population_manager.h
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
 	int	 GetWaveNumber( void ) { return m_iCurrentWaveIndex; }
 	int GetTotalWaveCount( void ) { return m_waveVector.Count(); }
+	CWave *GetWave( int index ) { return m_waveVector.IsValidIndex( index ) ? m_waveVector[ index ] : NULL; }

 	// Check Points
 	void ClearCheckpoint( void );
